---
export const prerender = false;
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import FaqAccordion from "../../../components/FaqAccordion.astro";

const courseFaqItems = [
  {
    question: "Is there a free AI agent course?",
    answer: "Yes, several genuinely exist. Google and Kaggle have both run free multi-day AI agent programs covering fundamentals at no cost, and major AI providers publish free agent-building documentation and tutorials. Free resources cover the fundamentals well. Where they fall short is anything role-specific or tied to your company's actual systems, which is what this page and our private training cover.",
  },
  {
    question: "What's covered in programs like Google's or Kaggle's 5-day AI agent courses?",
    answer: "These are real, well-regarded free programs, typically covering agent fundamentals, tool use, and hands-on exercises over a structured multi-day format. They're a legitimate starting point and worth doing if you want a free, structured introduction. This page doesn't replace them, it complements them with the practical, applied layer, and the careers guidance below, that a fundamentals-focused free program doesn't cover.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is this the same as an agentic AI course?",
    answer: "Related but not identical. Our Agentic AI Course covers the broader technical and conceptual skill of building agentic systems. This page uses \"AI agent\" the way most searchers mean it, as a specific skill and, further down this page, a specific career path, with less emphasis on the deeper orchestration concepts covered in the Agentic AI Course.",
  },
];

const careersFaqItems = [
  {
    question: "What does an AI agent specialist actually do day to day?",
    answer: "In practice, it's a mix of designing what an agent should do, building and testing it in a no-code or code-based tool, and monitoring how it performs against real inputs once it's live. It's closer to a hybrid of product thinking and technical implementation than pure engineering, and the exact mix varies a lot by employer.",
  },
  {
    question: "What salary can I expect for AI agent roles?",
    answer: "This varies enormously by location, seniority, and whether the role is full-time employment or contract work, and any specific number quoted online should be treated with caution given how new and fast-moving this job category is. Rather than quote a precise figure we can't verify, the honest guidance is: research current listings in your specific market and compare against adjacent roles like automation specialist or AI engineer, which tend to be more established comparison points.",
  },
  {
    question: "What do interviewers usually ask?",
    answer: "Expect a mix of conceptual questions (how would you decide what to automate versus keep manual) and practical ones (walk me through an agent you've built, what went wrong, how did you fix it). Having one or two real projects you can describe in detail, including a failure and what you learned, tends to matter more than reciting definitions.",
  },
  {
    question: "Are AI agent jobs available remotely?",
    answer: "Many are, particularly at smaller companies and agencies building agent-based products, since the work itself is typically done on a computer with no location requirement. That said, remote availability varies by employer and region, and it's worth verifying on each specific listing rather than assuming remote is standard across the field.",
  },
];

const faqLdJson = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [...courseFaqItems, ...careersFaqItems].map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.question,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.answer },
  })),
};

const courseLdJson = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Course',
  name: "AI Agent Course",
  description: "An AI agent course covering agent fundamentals, hands-on practice, free learning pathways, and a full careers guide covering AI agent jobs, salaries, and interview prep.",
  provider: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Lenoo AI', sameAs: 'https://lenooai.com' },
  url: 'https://lenooai.com/services/ai-courses/ai-agents',
};

const breadcrumbLdJson = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://lenooai.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Services', item: 'https://lenooai.com/services' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'AI Courses', item: 'https://lenooai.com/services/ai-courses' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 4, name: 'AI Agent Course', item: 'https://lenooai.com/services/ai-courses/ai-agents' },
  ],
};

Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', 's-maxage=60, stale-while-revalidate=300');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="AI Agent Course: Learn to Build AI Agents, Plus Careers Guide | Lenoo AI"
  description="An AI agent course covering fundamentals, free learning paths, and a full careers guide: AI agent jobs, salary expectations, and common interview questions."
  canonicalPath="/services/ai-courses/ai-agents"
  ldJson={[faqLdJson, courseLdJson, breadcrumbLdJson]}
>

<!-- ── HERO ── -->
<header class="hero-section" style="padding-top: 10rem; padding-bottom: 5rem; text-align: center;">
  <div class="container" style="position: relative; z-index: 1;">
    <div style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:rgba(0,227,253,0.12);border:1px solid rgba(0,227,253,0.28);border-radius:100px;padding:6px 16px;color:#a8f2ff;font-size:0.875rem;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:1.5rem;" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;opacity:0.65;">Home</a><span style="opacity:0.4;padding:0 4px;"> / </span><a href="/services" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;opacity:0.65;">Services</a><span style="opacity:0.4;padding:0 4px;"> / </span><a href="/services/ai-courses" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;opacity:0.65;">AI Courses</a><span style="opacity:0.4;padding:0 4px;"> / </span>AI Agent Course</div>
    <h1 style="max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto 1.5rem;">
      AI Agent <span class="gradient-text">Course</span> and Careers Guide
    </h1>
    <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.72); font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.75; max-width: 40rem; margin: 0 auto 0;">
      This page covers two things people search for under the same phrase: how to learn to build AI agents, and what a career in this space actually looks like, salaries, interview questions, and how to break in. Jump to whichever part you need.
    </p>
    <div class="trust-chips" style="justify-content:center; margin:1.75rem 0 2rem;">
      <span class="tchip">Course fundamentals and free pathways</span>
      <span class="tchip">Honest careers and salary guidance</span>
      <span class="tchip">No inflated promises either way</span>
    </div>
    <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; justify-content: center;">
      <a href="#course" class="btn-primary" style="font-size: 1rem;">Learn the Course →</a>
      <a href="#careers" class="btn-outline" style="font-size: 1rem;">Explore Careers →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ═══════════ PART 1: COURSE ═══════════ -->

<!-- ── WHAT THE COURSE COVERS ── -->
<section id="course" class="section" aria-labelledby="course-heading">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 800px;">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <p style="color: #006875; font-size: .8rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Part 1</p>
      <h2 id="course-heading">AI Agent Course: What to Actually Learn</h2>
    </div>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85; margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
      An "AI agent," in practical terms, is a system built to complete a task with some degree of independence: checking a data source, making a decision based on rules or judgment, and taking an action, rather than waiting for a person to prompt each individual step. Learning to build them is one of the more in-demand practical AI skills right now, and it's approachable without a traditional software engineering background.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85; margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
      A genuinely useful AI agent course covers both the concepts, what makes something an agent rather than a simple chatbot, and hands-on practice actually building one. Reading about agents without building anything leaves you unable to evaluate real opportunities or speak credibly about the work in an interview, which matters if you're approaching this from the careers angle covered further down this page.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85;">
      This page assumes no prior experience with agent-building specifically, though basic comfort with AI tools like ChatGPT or Claude helps. If you're starting from zero on AI generally, our <a href="/services/ai-courses/generative-ai" style="color:#006875; font-weight:600;">Generative AI Course</a> is worth doing first.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── CURRICULUM ── -->
<section class="section" style="background: #e7eeff;" aria-labelledby="curriculum-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <p style="color: #006875; font-size: .8rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; margin-bottom: 1rem;">What You'll Learn</p>
      <h2 id="curriculum-heading">Core Curriculum</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="path-grid">
      <div class="value-card path-card">
        <h3 style="font-size:1.0625rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.75rem; color:#00253b;">Agent Fundamentals</h3>
        <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:0.9375rem; line-height:1.7;">What separates an agent from a simple prompt-response tool: goal-directed behavior, multi-step planning, and the ability to use external tools rather than just generating text.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card path-card">
        <h3 style="font-size:1.0625rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.75rem; color:#00253b;">Hands-On Building Practice</h3>
        <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:0.9375rem; line-height:1.7;">Building a real, working agent for a narrow, well-defined task, using a no-code or low-code builder so the concepts matter more than syntax.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card path-card">
        <h3 style="font-size:1.0625rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.75rem; color:#00253b;">Tool Use and Integrations</h3>
        <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:0.9375rem; line-height:1.7;">Connecting an agent to external data and actions: checking a spreadsheet, calling an API, sending a message, so it can actually do something in the world, not just talk about it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card path-card">
        <h3 style="font-size:1.0625rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.75rem; color:#00253b;">Testing and Debugging Agents</h3>
        <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:0.9375rem; line-height:1.7;">Working through why an agent took an unexpected action, a skill that separates people who can genuinely build agents from people who can only follow a tutorial.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card path-card">
        <h3 style="font-size:1.0625rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.75rem; color:#00253b;">Portfolio-Building</h3>
        <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:0.9375rem; line-height:1.7;">Turning your practice projects into something you can actually describe and demonstrate, since this matters whether you're applying that skill at your current job or applying for a new role.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card path-card">
        <h3 style="font-size:1.0625rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.75rem; color:#00253b;">Where This Fits at Work</h3>
        <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:0.9375rem; line-height:1.7;">Recognizing which tasks in your own job or industry are genuinely good candidates for an agent versus which ones still need a person, so the skill translates into something useful immediately.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── FREE PATHWAYS ── -->
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="free-heading">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 800px;">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <h2 id="free-heading">Free Learning Pathways Worth Knowing About</h2>
    </div>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85; margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
      Two free programs come up often in searches for this topic, and both are legitimate: Google has run a free multi-day AI agent learning program, and Kaggle, the data science platform, has run a similar free five-day structured course. Both cover real fundamentals and hands-on exercises, and we're not affiliated with either, just pointing to genuinely useful free resources rather than pretending they don't exist.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85;">
      What these free programs are less likely to cover is the applied, role-specific layer: how agent-building connects to your particular job or industry, and the careers guidance in the second half of this page. Treat them as a strong, free foundation, and treat the rest of this page as what comes next.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── LEARN VS BUILD ── -->
<section class="section" style="background: #f0f3ff;" aria-labelledby="build-vs-learn-heading">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 800px;">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <h2 id="build-vs-learn-heading">Learning the Skill vs. Having an Agent Built for You</h2>
    </div>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85; margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
      This course, and the free resources mentioned above, teach you to build agents yourself. That's the right path if your goal is personal skill-building, prototyping your own ideas, or preparing for the career path covered in Part 2.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85;">
      If you're a business owner or manager who wants a production agent built into your company's actual systems, monitored and maintained properly, that's a development engagement rather than a course. Our <a href="/services/ai-agents" style="color:#006875; font-weight:600;">AI agent development service</a> covers that, and plenty of people take this course first specifically to understand what's realistic before commissioning custom work.
    </p>
    <div style="text-align:center;margin-top:2rem;padding:2rem;background:#ffffff;border-radius:20px;max-width:640px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;">
      <p style="color:#00253b;font-weight:700;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Covered by our 100% refund guarantee</p>
      <p style="color:#42474e;font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Want your team learning this together, or want us to build one for you?</p>
      <button onclick="openModal(this)" data-source="courses_ai_agents_course_mid" class="btn-primary">Request Training Quote →</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── COURSE FAQ ── -->
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="course-faq-heading">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 48rem;">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <h2 id="course-faq-heading">Course FAQ</h2>
    </div>
    <FaqAccordion items={courseFaqItems} />
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════ PART 2: CAREERS ═══════════ -->

<!-- ── CAREERS INTRO ── -->
<section id="careers" class="section" style="background: #e7eeff;" aria-labelledby="careers-heading">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 800px;">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <p style="color: #006875; font-size: .8rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Part 2</p>
      <h2 id="careers-heading">AI Agent Careers: Jobs, Salaries, and How to Break In</h2>
    </div>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85; margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
      This section is purely informational, a guide to the job market and how to prepare for it. It's not a live job board, and it isn't tied to any specific openings. If you're specifically interested in working with Lenoo AI, our own current openings live at <a href="/careers" style="color:#006875; font-weight:600;">our careers page</a>, separate from this general market overview.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85;">
      "AI agent" as a job title is still relatively new and inconsistently defined across companies. Some roles are titled exactly that. Others cover the same work under titles like automation engineer, AI implementation specialist, or applied AI engineer. It's worth searching broadly rather than only for the exact phrase "AI agent job."
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── JOB MARKET OVERVIEW ── -->
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="market-heading">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 800px;">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <h2 id="market-heading">The Job Market, Honestly</h2>
    </div>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85; margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
      Demand for people who can build and manage AI agents has grown quickly as more companies look to automate multi-step processes rather than just add a chatbot. That growth has happened faster than the job market has settled into consistent titles, expectations, or pay bands, which means the field currently rewards demonstrable skill more than credentials.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85; margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
      Roles show up across a wide range of company types: dedicated AI agencies building agents for clients, in-house roles at companies automating their own operations, and freelance or contract work for businesses that need one specific agent built rather than an ongoing hire. Each of these has a different hiring bar and a different day-to-day reality.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85;">
      Geographically, opportunities are not evenly distributed, and search volume data suggests meaningful interest from markets including India alongside global remote-friendly postings. Whichever market you're in, the practical advice is the same: build something real, be able to explain it clearly, and search broadly across adjacent job titles.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── SALARY ── -->
<section class="section" style="background: #f0f3ff;" aria-labelledby="salary-heading">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 800px;">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <h2 id="salary-heading">Salary Expectations</h2>
    </div>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85; margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
      We're not going to quote a precise salary figure here, and any page that does for a job category this new and this inconsistently titled should be treated with some skepticism. Pay varies enormously by location, company size, seniority, and whether the role is full-time, contract, or freelance project work.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85; margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
      A more reliable approach than trusting a single quoted number: look at current listings in your specific market and compare against more established, adjacent roles, automation specialist, AI engineer, or software developer with AI experience, since those categories have more historical salary data to benchmark against.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85;">
      Freelance and contract AI agent work is also common, priced per project rather than as a salary, and rates there vary just as widely based on project complexity and the client's budget.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── INTERVIEW QUESTIONS ── -->
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="interview-heading">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 800px;">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <h2 id="interview-heading">Common Interview Questions</h2>
    </div>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85; margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
      Interviews for AI agent roles tend to mix conceptual and practical questions. A few that come up often, along with what interviewers are usually probing for:
    </p>
    <div class="path-grid">
      <div class="value-card path-card">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.5rem; color:#00253b;">"Walk me through an agent you've built."</h3>
        <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:0.9375rem; line-height:1.7;">They want a specific, real example, not a hypothetical. Having one or two projects you can describe in real detail matters more than broad familiarity with many tools.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card path-card">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.5rem; color:#00253b;">"What went wrong, and how did you fix it?"</h3>
        <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:0.9375rem; line-height:1.7;">A polished success story with no failures raises doubts. Being honest about a mistake and how you diagnosed it signals real hands-on experience.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card path-card">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.5rem; color:#00253b;">"How do you decide what to automate versus keep manual?"</h3>
        <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:0.9375rem; line-height:1.7;">This tests judgment, not just technical skill. A good answer references stability, risk, and how well-defined the task is.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card path-card">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.5rem; color:#00253b;">"How do you handle errors or unexpected input?"</h3>
        <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:0.9375rem; line-height:1.7;">This probes whether you think about failure modes, not just the happy path, which is a common gap in self-taught candidates.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card path-card">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.5rem; color:#00253b;">"What tools and platforms have you used?"</h3>
        <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:0.9375rem; line-height:1.7;">Be honest about your actual experience level with each. Overstating familiarity tends to unravel quickly in a technical follow-up.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card path-card">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.5rem; color:#00253b;">"How would you explain this to a non-technical stakeholder?"</h3>
        <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:0.9375rem; line-height:1.7;">Many AI agent roles involve working with business teams, not just engineers. Clear, jargon-free explanation is a real, tested skill.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── HOW TO BREAK IN ── -->
<section class="section" style="background: #f0f3ff;" aria-labelledby="break-in-heading">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 800px;">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <h2 id="break-in-heading">How to Break In</h2>
    </div>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85; margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
      For freshers and career-changers, the single most useful thing you can do is build two or three real agents, even small ones, and document them clearly: what problem they solved, how you built them, what went wrong, and what you'd do differently. This matters more than any certificate, since it's concrete proof you can do the work, not just describe it.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85; margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
      Volunteer to build a small automation for a local business, a nonprofit, or even your own household tasks if nothing else is available. A real, working project beats a tutorial-following exercise every time in an interview conversation.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85;">
      When applying, search beyond the exact phrase "AI agent" to related titles like automation specialist, AI implementation engineer, or workflow automation developer, since the same underlying skill set is often listed under different names depending on the company.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── REMOTE WORK REALITY CHECK ── -->
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="remote-heading">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 800px;">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <h2 id="remote-heading">Remote Work: The Reality Check</h2>
    </div>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85; margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
      A meaningful share of AI agent roles are remote-friendly, since the work itself typically doesn't require being in a specific physical location. That said, "remote available" varies significantly by employer, and some companies restrict remote hiring to specific countries or time zones for legal and tax reasons.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.85;">
      Always verify remote eligibility on the specific listing rather than assuming it applies broadly, and be cautious of postings that seem to promise unusually high pay for fully remote, no-experience-required AI agent work, since that pattern shows up in low-quality or misleading listings across many emerging tech fields, not just this one.
    </p>
    <div style="text-align:center;margin-top:2rem;padding:2rem;background:#ffffff;border-radius:20px;max-width:640px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;">
      <p style="color:#00253b;font-weight:700;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Building your skills for this career path?</p>
      <p style="color:#42474e;font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">If you'd rather build this skill with structured, private guidance than entirely on your own, we can help. And if you're interested in working with us specifically, see our own openings.</p>
      <div style="display:flex; gap:1rem; justify-content:center; flex-wrap:wrap;">
        <button onclick="openModal(this)" data-source="courses_ai_agents_careers_cta" class="btn-primary">Request Training Quote →</button>
        <a href="/careers" class="btn-outline">See Our Openings →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── CAREERS FAQ ── -->
<section class="section" style="background: #e7eeff;" aria-labelledby="careers-faq-heading">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 48rem;">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
